libgcc: use soft-fp instead of fp-bit for sh*-elf

sh-elf still used fp-bit, the old generic C soft-float.  Switch it to
soft-fp, like most soft-float targets: add config/sh/sfp-machine.h
(umul_ppmm is dmulu.l and udiv_qrnnd is __udiv_qrnnd_16, both from
longlong.h) and use t-softfp-sfdf t-softfp-excl t-softfp in config.host.
t-softfp-excl keeps the libgcc2.c DImode conversions, so multilibs with
an FPU keep using it for those.  Single-precision division uses
_FP_DIV_MEAT_1_udiv_norm: the bit loop other ports use was slower than
fp-bit here.

Cycles per call on sh-elf -m2 (GDB SH simulator, normal operands):

          fp-bit  soft-fp
    fadd     252      163    1.5x
    fmul     203      140    1.5x
    fdiv     452      218    2.1x
    fcmp     136       63    2.2x
    i2f      134       99    1.4x
    f2i       74       43    1.7x
    dadd     414      244    1.7x
    dmul     341      230    1.5x
    ddiv    1049      391    2.7x
    dcmp     153       64    2.4x
    i2d      160      106    1.5x
    d2i       88       47    1.9x
    f2d      148       45    3.3x
    d2f      132       88    1.5x

It is also more accurate: 688,846 results of +, -, *, /, compares and
conversions on random and special operands (NaN, Inf, denormals,
cancellation) match an x86-64 host bit for bit, while fp-bit gets six
wrong (denormal results of mul and div, one ulp off).
gcc.c-torture/execute/ieee at -O0/-O1/-O2/-Os and gcc.c-torture/execute
at -O2: identical results with fp-bit and soft-fp.

Cost: soft-fp inlines unpacking and packing into each function, so code
grows.  .text of a program using float add, mul and compare: +1.5 KB;
the same with double: +2.0 KB; one using every operation: +9.6 KB.
fp-bit's __cmpsf2/__cmpdf2 and its internal helpers (__pack_f,
__unpack_d, ...) are gone; GCC does not emit calls to them.

Not tested: little-endian (-ml), SH1 (-m1, which gets the generic C
umul_ppmm) and the FPU multilibs.

Ported to 14.2.0 (same change; libgcc built by this branch's compiler),
sh-elf -m2 on the GDB SH simulator: gcc.c-torture/execute/ieee at
-O0/-O1/-O2/-Os: same results with fp-bit and soft-fp.  A differential
test of 131,031 float and double results (+, -, *, /, compares and
conversions, random and special operands) matches an x86-64 host bit for
bit with soft-fp; fp-bit gets 4 wrong (denormal multiplies, one ulp
off).

libgcc/ChangeLog:

	* config.host (sh-*-elf*, sh[12346l]*-*-elf*): Use soft-fp
	instead of fp-bit.
	* config/sh/sfp-machine.h: New file.

--- a/gcc-14.2.0/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/gcc-14.2.0/libgcc/config.host
@@ -1401,7 +1401,7 @@
 	md_unwind_header=s390/tpf-unwind.h
 	;;
 sh-*-elf* | sh[12346l]*-*-elf*)
-	tmake_file="$tmake_file sh/t-sh t-crtstuff-pic t-fdpbit"
+	tmake_file="$tmake_file sh/t-sh t-crtstuff-pic t-softfp-sfdf t-softfp-excl t-softfp"
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crt1.o crti.o crtn.o crtbeginS.o crtendS.o \
 		libic_invalidate_array_4-100.a \
 		libic_invalidate_array_4-200.a \
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc-14.2.0/libgcc/config/sh/sfp-machine.h
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
